tone of voice means the way your voice sounds, showing your feelings.

21
00:01:10.952 --> 00:01:13.080
Her tone of voice showed she was upset.

22
00:01:13.780 --> 00:01:16.235
Your turn. Say: tone of voice.

23
00:01:18.935 --> 00:01:20.261
tone of voice.

24
00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:22.518
small disagreement.

25
00:01:23.218 --> 00:01:25.937
small disagreement means a minor difference of opinion.

26
00:01:26.237 --> 00:01:28.748
We had a small disagreement about where to eat.

27
00:01:29.448 --> 00:01:32.390
Your turn. Say: small disagreement.

28
00:01:35.090 --> 00:01:36.463
small disagreement.

29
00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:38.579
open-minded.

30
00:01:39.279 --> 00:01:42.660
open-minded means willing to listen to new ideas.

31
00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:45.842
Try to be open-minded when people disagree with you.

32
00:01:46.542 --> 00:01:49.473
Your turn. Say: open-minded.

33
00:01:52.173 --> 00:01:53.453
open-minded.

34
00:01:54.450 --> 00:01:55.347
respond.

35
00:01:56.047 --> 00:01:58.209
respond means to answer or react.

36
00:01:58.509 --> 00:02:01.042
He didn't respond to my message for two days.

37
00:02:01.742 --> 00:02:03.756
Your turn. Say: respond.

38
00:02:06.456 --> 00:02:07.469
respond.

39
00:02:08.483 --> 00:02:09.868
express an opinion.

40
00:02:10.568 --> 00:02:13.322
express an opinion means to say what you think.

41
00:02:13.622 --> 00:02:16.504
Don't be afraid to express an opinion in class.

42
00:02:17.204 --> 00:02:20.135
Your turn. Say: express an opinion.

43
00:02:22.835 --> 00:02:24.381
express an opinion.

44
00:02:25.383 --> 00:02:27.348
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:27.648 --> 00:02:30.518
I had a small disagreement with my group yesterday.

46
00:02:31.817 --> 00:02:32.667
What happened?

47
00:02:33.983 --> 00:02:37.492
I wanted to express an opinion, but nobody stopped talking.

48
00:02:38.783 --> 00:02:42.283
Try asking them to listen. And avoid raising your tone of voice.

49
00:02:43.583 --> 00:02:46.094
I promise to stay calm and open-minded.

50
00:02:47.383 --> 00:02:51.290
Good. Active listening means letting others finish before you respond.

51
00:02:52.583 --> 00:02:55.988
Grammar focus: Gerund vs infinitive.

52
00:02:56.288 --> 00:02:59.924
Some verbs are followed by the -ing form, like enjoy, avoid and keep.

53
00:03:00.224 --> 00:03:03.989
Others are followed by to plus verb, like want, decide and promise.

54
00:03:04.289 --> 00:03:08.450
For example: I enjoy talking to people. He decided to apologise.

55
00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:12.445
After prepositions, always use the -ing form: I'm good at listening.

56
00:03:13.450 --> 00:03:16.184
Now read and listen. Listen More, Talk Less.

57
00:03:16.484 --> 00:03:19.644
Most people think good communication means speaking well.

58
00:03:20.950 --> 00:03:25.028
In fact, researchers say that active listening is even more important.

59
00:03:26.317 --> 00:03:29.663
Good listeners avoid interrupting and keep asking questions.

60
00:03:30.950 --> 00:03:34.366
Body posture and tone of voice also send strong messages.

61
00:03:35.650 --> 00:03:39.089
If you decide to listen first, you will have fewer misunderstandings.

62
00:03:40.383 --> 00:03:42.687
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

63
00:03:42.987 --> 00:03:45.289
Willing to listen to new ideas is blank.

64
00:03:45.589 --> 00:03:49.358
A, open-minded. B, misunderstanding. C, respond.

65
00:03:53.350 --> 00:03:55.768
The answer is A: open-minded.

66
00:03:57.283 --> 00:03:59.364
I enjoy blank with my friends.

67
00:03:59.664 --> 00:04:02.714
A, to chat. B, chatting. C, chat.

68
00:04:06.717 --> 00:04:08.438
The answer is B: chatting.

69
00:04:09.950 --> 00:04:11.822
She decided blank a new course.

70
00:04:12.122 --> 00:04:15.137
A, taking. B, to take. C, take.

71
00:04:19.150 --> 00:04:20.836
The answer is B: to take.

72
00:04:22.350 --> 00:04:24.187
The way your voice sounds is your blank.

73
00:04:24.487 --> 00:04:28.373
A, body posture. B, tone of voice. C, active listening.

74
00:04:32.383 --> 00:04:34.406
The answer is B: tone of voice.

75
00:04:35.917 --> 00:04:39.031
According to the text, good listeners avoid blank.

76
00:04:39.331 --> 00:04:43.332
A, asking questions. B, interrupting. C, smiling.

77
00:04:47.317 --> 00:04:49.351
The answer is B: interrupting.

78
00:04:50.850 --> 00:04:54.512
Now it's your turn to speak. How do you handle a disagreement with a friend?

79
00:04:59.812 --> 00:05:04.622
I try to listen first, avoid shouting and then explain my opinion calmly.

80
00:05:04.922 --> 00:05:06.317
Excellent answer, Nita!

81
00:05:07.317 --> 00:05:11.490
Great work today! You learned eight new words and gerund vs infinitive.

82
00:05:11.790 --> 00:05:15.162
Today's value is respect. Thank the people who help us.

83
00:05:15.462 --> 00:05:17.824
See you in Unit fourteen. Goodbye!

84
00:05:18.124 --> 00:05:20.916
Thank you, Mr. Daniel! Bye, everyone!

